# gentoo-install — package set: init-systemd
# inherits: -
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Overlaid on the chosen set when --init systemd, and deliberately empty.
#
# systemd-journald is the system log and systemd timers are the cron, both
# already part of @system on a systemd profile. Adding syslog-ng or cronie
# beside them gives the machine two of each, with the logs split across the
# two and no error anywhere to say so.
#
# The file exists rather than being absent because "nothing to add" is an
# answer, and an empty file makes the asymmetry with init-openrc.list visible
# to whoever reads data/packages/sets.tsv.
#
# One atom per line, # starts a comment.
